 ( { Which is best: } 0... gxf6 0. d5 { (grabbing space) or } 1. dxe5 { (exchanging central pawns)? } ) 
1. { -KEY- } dxe5 $1 { Correct! By playing in this way White kills the potential outpost on d4 for Black's knight. } ( 1. d5 $2 { turns out to be a big mistake, since Black can reply with } Nd4 $1 { when after } 2. Qd1 Nb3 3. Rb1 b5 $17 { Black's initiative bought them time to secure their extra pawn on c4. } ) 
Nxe5 2. Nxe5 Bxe5 3. Bxc4 $14 { White is left with a slight edge here, owing to their unopposed central pawn on e4. In the long run they may try to advance with f2-f4 followed by e4-e5, activating their dangerous kingside pawn majority. } 
