 ( { White has greater central control, but it is currently under attack. Choose between } 0... Nc6 0. d5 { and } 1. dxe5 { . } ) 
1. { -KEY- } dxe5 $1 { Correct! White gives up their ideal centre, but in exchange they keep an advantage due to their superior minor pieces. } ( 1. d5 $2 { Grabbing space is optically appealing, but has two major downsides relating to both side's knights. In White's case, they would lose the d5 outpost while the Black counterpart would gain access to the c5 square. } ) 
Nxe5 ( 1... dxe5 $6 { Black would not be wise to recapture with the pawn here, since now the a1-h8 diagonal is shut down and their bishop locked out of the play. } ) 
2. Nxe5 Bxe5 3. Nd5 $16 { White has a slight edge with the better structure and the more effective minor piece. ...Bxb2 is not a concern due to Ra1-b1 followed by capturing on b7. } 
