 { Black is down a pawn but has pressure in the centre. White can hope for a slight advantage after Nf3-h4, but they have an even stronger move. Can you find it? } 16. { -KEY- } d4 $1 { Counter-attacking the knight on c5, and grabbing some space in the centre. } ( 16. Nh4 $6 { is also playable, but after } Rd8 { White will have nothing better than to play } 17. d4 { , when after } exd3 18. cxd3 $13 { they get an inferior version of the game continuation. } ) 
exf3 { Black has nothing better than to accept the exchange of knights. } ( 16... exd3 $2 { is not a concern, since now after } 17. cxd3 $16 { White's structure is not worse than the opponent's, while they remain up a pawn. } ) 
