 { This position is taken from the online game Carlsen,M - Theodorou,N (2023) . Find the best sequence for Black. } 1... { -KEY- } exd4 $1 2. cxd4 ( 2. Bxd4 Nxd4 3. cxd4 c5 $11 { The bishop pair combined with the continued pressure against the centre allows Black to equalise. } ) 
 ( 2. Nxd4 Nxd4 3. Bxd4 c5 $1 { Since Bd4-e3 will be met by ...Nxe4, White is forced to capture on f6. } 4. Bxf6 Qxf6 $11 { Black has a hole on d5, but on the other hand they have defused the pressure in the centre and they have collected the bishop pair, ensuring a balanced struggle. } ) 
Nb4 $1 { Now the bishop on c2 has nowhere to run. } ( 2... Nxe4 $4 { An easy trap to fall for would be to capture the central pawn. } 3. d5 $1 Nb4 4. Bxa7 $18 { when Black is losing a piece. } ) 
3. Nc3 Nxc2 4. Qxc2 Nxe4 $1 5. Nxe4 Bf5 $1 { Correct! This was a very challenging sequence which required spotting several tricks and traps along the way. This concludes the puzzle section for this chapter - I'll see you in the next one! } 
